---
import AppStoreButton from './AppStoreButton.astro';
import { SOURCE_URL } from '../data';
---

<section id="get" class="relative py-24 sm:py-32">
  <div class="container-wide">
    <div class="relative overflow-hidden rounded-3xl border border-ink-700/80 bg-gradient-to-b from-ink-800/70 to-ink-900/60 p-10 shadow-card sm:p-16">
      <div class="grid-bg absolute inset-0" aria-hidden="true"></div>
      <div class="relative text-center">
        <span class="eyebrow">Join the conversation</span>
        <h2 class="mt-3 text-balance text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight sm:text-5xl">
          Get Arkhe.
        </h2>
        <p class="mx-auto mt-4 max-w-xl text-ink-300">
          One purchase, no subscription, no account, no tracking. Buying it on the App Store
          supports development; the source is open if you’d rather build it yourself.
        </p>

        <div class="mt-9 flex flex-col items-center justify-center gap-3 sm:flex-row">
          <AppStoreButton class="text-[15px]" />
          <a href={SOURCE_URL} target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="btn-ghost text-[15px]">View the source</a>
        </div>

        <dl class="mx-auto mt-10 grid max-w-3xl grid-cols-2 gap-6 text-left sm:grid-cols-4">
          <div>
            <dt class="font-mono text-[10px] uppercase tracking-widest text-ink-400">Devices</dt>
            <dd class="mt-1 text-sm text-ink-100">iPhone &amp; iPad</dd>
          </div>
          <div>
            <dt class="font-mono text-[10px] uppercase tracking-widest text-ink-400">Requires</dt>
            <dd class="mt-1 text-sm text-ink-100">iOS 17 or later</dd>
          </div>
          <div>
            <dt class="font-mono text-[10px] uppercase tracking-widest text-ink-400">Connects to</dt>
            <dd class="mt-1 text-sm text-ink-100">Any IRC network or bouncer</dd>
          </div>
          <div>
            <dt class="font-mono text-[10px] uppercase tracking-widest text-ink-400">License</dt>
            <dd class="mt-1 text-sm text-ink-100">Apache 2.0</dd>
          </div>
        </dl>

        <p class="mt-10 text-xs text-ink-500">
          Arkhe is a chat client: you need access to an IRC network or a bouncer. The
          <a href="/support" class="underline decoration-ink-600 underline-offset-2 hover:text-ink-300">support page</a>
          explains how to connect.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
